"request-key+++[]\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"[.description]\n"
"--\n"
"What the rule counts requests per: every distinct key gets its own `quarkus."
"http.rate-limit.rules.\"rule\".permits` per `quarkus.http.rate-limit.rules."
"\"rule\".window`. One of:\n"
"\n"
" * `ip`: the client address\n"
" * `principal`: the authenticated user. Only available after authentication; "
"a request without a non-anonymous identity is keyed by its client address, "
"like `ip`\n"
" * `header:<name>`: the value of that request header, stored hashed; a "
"request without it is keyed by its client address, and every request that "
"repeats it by one shared key\n"
" * `global`: one key for every request the rule matches\n"
" * `custom:<name>`: the `RateLimitKeyResolver` bean of the application "
"annotated `@Identifier(\"<name>\")`\n"
"\n"
"Defaults to `quarkus.http.rate-limit.request-key`; one of the two must be "
"set.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Environment variable: env_var_with_copy_button:"
"+++QUARKUS_HTTP_RATE_LIMIT_RULES__RULE__REQUEST_KEY+++[]\n"
"--"
