msgid ""
"[[quarkus-http-rate-limit_quarkus-http-rate-limit-rules-rule-lease-size]] [."
"property-path]##link:#quarkus-http-rate-limit_quarkus-http-rate-limit-rules-"
"rule-lease-size[`+++quarkus.http.rate-limit.rules.\"rule\".lease-size+++`]##\n"
"config_property_copy_button:+++quarkus.http.rate-limit.rules.\"rule\".lease-"
"size+++[]\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"[.description]\n"
"--\n"
"When set, the rule uses lease mode: it claims chunks of up to this many "
"permits from the store and serves requests from the chunk, trading admission "
"precision for fewer store calls. The actual chunk adapts to the demand of "
"this replica, and a chunk may be served for `lease-size` emission intervals "
"(`window / permits`). At least 1, and no more than a static limit's burst; "
"for resolved limits each chunk is capped to the selected burst. At most "
"`permits / 20` is recommended, because every replica may strand up to one "
"chunk. Requires a store other than `local`. When absent, every request makes "
"one store call.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Environment variable: env_var_with_copy_button:"
"+++QUARKUS_HTTP_RATE_LIMIT_RULES__RULE__LEASE_SIZE+++[]\n"
"--"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"[[quarkus-http-rate-limit_quarkus-http-rate-limit-rules-rule-lease-size]] [."
"property-path]##link:#quarkus-http-rate-limit_quarkus-http-rate-limit-rules-"
"rule-lease-size[`+++quarkus.http.rate-limit.rules.\"rule\".lease-size+++`]##\n"
"config_property_copy_button:+++quarkus.http.rate-limit.rules.\"rule\".lease-"
"size+++[]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When set, the rule uses lease mode: it claims chunks of up to this many "
"permits from the store and serves requests from the chunk, trading admission "
"precision for fewer store calls. The actual chunk adapts to the demand of "
"this replica, and a chunk may be served for `lease-size` emission intervals "
"(`window / permits`). At least 1, and no more than a static limit's burst; "
"for resolved limits each chunk is capped to the selected burst. At most "
"`permits / 20` is recommended, because every replica may strand up to one "
"chunk. Requires a store other than `local`. When absent, every request makes "
"one store call."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Environment variable: env_var_with_copy_button:"
"+++QUARKUS_HTTP_RATE_LIMIT_RULES__RULE__LEASE_SIZE+++[]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"[[quarkus-http-rate-limit_quarkus-http-rate-limit-rules-rule-max-overdraft]] "
"[.property-path]##link:#quarkus-http-rate-limit_quarkus-http-rate-limit-"
"rules-rule-max-overdraft[`+++quarkus.http.rate-limit.rules.\"rule\".max-"
"overdraft+++`]##\n"
"config_property_copy_button:+++quarkus.http.rate-limit.rules.\"rule\".max-"
"overdraft+++[]\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"[.description]\n"
"--\n"
"The number of requests per key that a replica may admit without holding "
"permits, per emission interval (`window / permits`), while it claims a chunk "
"from the store. `0` is strict: a request that finds no chunk waits for the "
"claim, at most the store timeout (`quarkus.http.rate-limit.store-timeout`, "
"or `quarkus.http.rate-limit.redis.timeout` for the `redis` store). Above `0` "
"is optimistic: up to this many requests per emission interval are admitted "
"at once and settled with the claim; when they are used up, or for a while "
"after the store refused a claim, requests wait as in strict mode. Admissions "
"that the store then refuses got through over the limit; they are forgiven, "
"and counted. Between 0 and a static limit's burst; capped to the selected "
"burst for resolved limits. Only valid with `lease-size`.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Environment variable: env_var_with_copy_button:"
"+++QUARKUS_HTTP_RATE_LIMIT_RULES__RULE__MAX_OVERDRAFT+++[]\n"
"--"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"[[quarkus-http-rate-limit_quarkus-http-rate-limit-rules-rule-max-overdraft]] "
"[.property-path]##link:#quarkus-http-rate-limit_quarkus-http-rate-limit-"
"rules-rule-max-overdraft[`+++quarkus.http.rate-limit.rules.\"rule\".max-"
"overdraft+++`]##\n"
"config_property_copy_button:+++quarkus.http.rate-limit.rules.\"rule\".max-"
"overdraft+++[]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The number of requests per key that a replica may admit without holding "
"permits, per emission interval (`window / permits`), while it claims a chunk "
"from the store. `0` is strict: a request that finds no chunk waits for the "
"claim, at most the store timeout (`quarkus.http.rate-limit.store-timeout`, "
"or `quarkus.http.rate-limit.redis.timeout` for the `redis` store). Above `0` "
"is optimistic: up to this many requests per emission interval are admitted "
"at once and settled with the claim; when they are used up, or for a while "
"after the store refused a claim, requests wait as in strict mode. Admissions "
"that the store then refuses got through over the limit; they are forgiven, "
"and counted. Between 0 and a static limit's burst; capped to the selected "
"burst for resolved limits. Only valid with `lease-size`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Environment variable: env_var_with_copy_button:"
"+++QUARKUS_HTTP_RATE_LIMIT_RULES__RULE__MAX_OVERDRAFT+++[]"
msgstr ""

